# Paths Semgrep should not scan.
#
# Semgrep's own defaults are NOT inherited once this file exists -- it replaces
# them -- so the standard ignores are restated below before anything is added.
# https://semgrep.dev/docs/ignoring-files-folders-code

# --- Semgrep defaults, restated (see note above) ---
#
# This list must stay COMPLETE. An earlier version restated only six entries,
# which silently DROPPED the rest -- measured: scan scope went from 630 files to
# 640, re-including all ten of `frontend/src/test/` because `test/` is a default
# this file had stopped honouring. A partial restatement does not narrow scope,
# it WIDENS it, which is the opposite of what an ignore file looks like it does.
#
# Verify after any edit here by comparing `paths.scanned` with and without the
# file; the counts must differ only by what this repository deliberately excludes
# below.
.git/
.hg/
.svn/
_darcs/
CVS/
node_modules/
vendor/
.npm/
.yarn/
.venv/
.env/
.tox/
_opam/
_build/
_cargo/
dist/
build/
coverage/
test/
tests/
testsuite/
*_test.go
*.min.js

