# Security-review reference material. These documents exist to SHOW vulnerable
# patterns so a reviewer can recognise them -- `User.objects.raw(f"SELECT ...")`
# is annotated `# SQLi` in the source. Semgrep read them as six HIGH-severity
# SQL-injection findings, which were the loudest results in the account and
# every one a false positive.
#
# This matters more than the count suggests: the findings are moving from the
# Rule Board's Audit column (dashboard-only, no PR comments) to Comment, and
# six confident false HIGHs on every PR is how a reviewer learns to skim the
# actionable bucket. Same failure as the streaming-link audit in #871.
.github/skills/**/references/
